ulations> Title 47 - Telecommunication> CHAPTER I--FEDERAL COMMUNICATIONS COMMISSION> PART 76--MULTICHANNEL VIDEO AND CABLE TELEVISION SERVICE> Subpart M—Cable Inside Wiring\n\n### 47 C.F.R. Subpart M—Cable Inside Wiring\n\nTitle 47 - Telecommunication\n\nTitle 47: Telecommunication\nPART 76—MULTICHANNEL VIDEO AND CABLE TELEVISION SERVICE\n\n##### Subpart M—Cable Inside Wiring\n\n##### § 76.800   Definitions.\n\n(a) MDU. A multiple dwelling unit building (e.g., an apartment building, condominium building or cooperative).\n\n(b) MDU owner. The entity that owns or controls the common areas of a multiple dwelling unit building.\n\n(c) MVPD. A multichannel video programming distributor, as that term is defined in Section 602(13) of the Communications Act, 47 U.S.C. 522(13).\n\n(d) Home run wiring. The wiring from the demarcation point to the point at which the MVPD's wiring becomes devoted to an individual subscriber or individual loop.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFederal Register / Vol. 62, No. 220 / Friday, November 14, 1997 / Rules and Regulations 61031 (https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1997-11-14/pdf/FR-1997-11-14.pdf)\nciteturn2158search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.4 years ago; Part 76 of title 47 of the Code of Federal Regulations is amended as follows: ... Subpart M is amended by revising the heading to read as follows:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n47 C.F.R. Subpart M—Cable Operations and Licensing System (COALS) (https://chanrobles.com/usa/uslaws/cfr/title47/47-1.0.1.1.2.13.php)\nciteturn2158search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Subpart M—Cable Operations and Licensing System (COALS)Title 47 - Telecommunication ... Source:  68 FR 27001, May 19, 2003, unless otherwise noted. ... This subpart applies to filings required by §§76.403, 76.1610, 76.1801, 76.1803, & 76.1804, and 78.11 through 78.36 of this chapter.\n--------------------------